# Formation rate functions the axiom text admits: record-determined clocks reduce to the constant clock between neighbour records, and state-reading clocks split by menu dephasing

**Date:** 2026-09-24
**Type:** bounded_theorem
**Status:** exact finite certificates under supplied decision points; unaudited.

## Result

The landed note
`RECORD_FORMATION_CLOCK_IN_THE_CLAUSE_THE_FIELD_ALIGNED_MENU_S_ODDS_DO_NOT_DEPEND_ON_WHEN_RECORDS_FORM_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md`
supplied a formation clock whose rate is a function of the site's pre-record
conditional state and left open which rate function the axioms favour. This
note reads the axiom text against five classes of rate function and proves
the small exact statements that separate them. Nothing is adopted.

- **The text admits every class and fixes none.** Admissibility's reading
  note says of the distribution that "it does not supply the formation site,
  probability, or rate"; the open-gates list keeps "the remaining formation
  rules (the distribution's form and values, at which site, and at what
  rate)" outside the axioms. Every candidate rate is downstream supplier
  content.
- **Record-determined rates are constant between neighbour records.** A rate
  that is a functional of the law-level distribution, or of the neighbours'
  records directly, changes only when a neighbour's record forms. Between
  such events it is the constant clock of the landed note at a
  record-dependent value, and every constant-clock identity carries over. On
  the isolated site the three functionals tried give odds identical to the
  constant clock at their value to 0e+00, on both menus and in the two-qubit
  model.
- **A precise register criterion separates the classes.** Call a rate
  registered-only when it is invariant under the menu dephasing channel
  `ρ → P₊ρP₊ + P₋ρP₋`, so that it depends on the site only through the menu
  odds `Tr(P_q ρ)`. Constant, law, odds and alignment clocks pass (deviation
  at most 9e-16); the purity and coherence clocks fail (0.991). A witness pair
  on a menu perpendicular to the field, with identical menu odds at every
  time and different menu coherence, gets identical odds from every
  registered-only clock and different odds from the purity clock (0.6126
  against 0.5547) and the coherence clock (0.7165 against 0.6905).
- **The constant clock has a closed form.** On the precessing isolated site
  the recorded odds on any menu are the trace rule of the Laplace-transformed
  Bloch vector, `r_f = r_∥ + f²/(f²+ω²) r_⊥ + fω/(f²+ω²) ĥ×r_⊥`. A fast
  clock records the initial odds; a slow clock records the odds of the
  field-dephased state. The landed values 0.8437 and 0.8154 are this formula.
- **Covariance and the register criterion are independent cuts.** The landed
  covariant menu-axis span `{1, |r|², (r·n)²}` contains `|r|² − (r·n)² =
  4|ρ₊₋|²`, a covariant rate that reads the coherence. Covariance alone does
  not settle the question the landed note left open; the register reading
  does, and it is a reading.

So the axiom text, read literally, leaves the rate function to the supplier;
read with "A site with no record cannot be read" extended to the formation
process (D-register), it admits the constant and record-determined classes
without further structure and marks the state-reading class as the one whose
clock reads an unrecorded site. Which reading holds is not decided here.

