## What this means for the lanes

- **Record formation.** The landed note's open item, which rate function the
  axioms favour, splits: the text favours none; covariance removes labelled
  functionals but keeps a coherence-reading rate; the register reading
  D-register separates the classes, and it is a reading. Under it the
  constant and record-determined classes cost only a number or a
  relabelling-invariant functional, and between neighbour records they are
  the constant clock whose identities are landed.
- **The tick.** A record-determined rate makes the mean interval between
  formations at a site `1/F(p(·|R))`, a function of the neighbours' records:
  the unit of emergent time varies with the record pattern, as in the landed
  value-dependent clocks of
  `ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_FORMATION_RATE_IDENTITIES_AND_FINITE_WINDOW_WITNESSES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-15.md`,
  whose value-blind clocks are D-form-const and whose value-dependent clocks
  are D-form-records here. A state-reading rate makes the tick read the
  coherence even where the odds do not (Theorem 2(c), field menu).
- **The Admissibility sentence.** D-form-odds needs the identification of
  `Tr(P_q ρ)` with the law's odds; the landed note's caveat that the
  field-menu odds depend on the supplied initial component `r₀·ĥ` applies to
  it unchanged. D-form-law does not need the identification.

